-- title:
--   Cotangent length bound along a surjection of deformation rings
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain and is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, that is, a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (realised as the automorphism group of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$) on a space of rank $2$ whose associated homomorphism becomes trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $\mathcal{D}_0$ and $\mathcal{D}'$ be two deformation conditions, i.e. predicates on adic Galois representations over local $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, and let $D_0$, $D'$ be deformation-ring data for $\bar\rho$ and $\mathcal{D}_0$, resp. $\mathcal{D}'$: each consists of a complete noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $R$ with local structure map and residue field generated by the image of $\mathcal{O}$, a representation $\rho$ over $R$ satisfying the condition, whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ (which is assumed absolutely irreducible), together with the universal property of $R$ for such deformations; only the underlying $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $D_0.R$ and $D'.R$ enter the statement. Let $\theta : D'.R \to D_0.R$ be a surjective $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map, $x_0 : D_0.R \to \mathcal{O}$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map, and write $I_0 = \ker x_0$, $I' = \ker (x_0 \circ \theta)$, with cotangent modules $I_0/I_0^2$ and $I'/I'^2$; let $\Phi$ denote the kernel of the induced map $I'/I'^2 \to I_0/I_0^2$. Let $B \in \mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$ and suppose that for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ the $\mathcal{O}$-length of the quotient of $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathcal{O}}(I'/I'^2, \mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}^{n+1})$ by the submodule of homomorphisms vanishing on $\Phi$ (the kernel of restriction along the inclusion of $\Phi$) is at most $B$. Then the $\mathcal{O}$-length of $I'/I'^2$ is at most the $\mathcal{O}$-length of $I_0/I_0^2$ plus $B$, lengths and the sum being taken in $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$.
--
--   This is the length-counting step used when comparing the cotangent space of a universal deformation ring at an $\mathcal{O}$-point with that of the deformation ring for a more restrictive condition mapping onto it: a bound, uniform in the level $n$, on the image of restriction to the relative cotangent kernel in $\mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}^{n+1}$-valued functionals yields an additive bound on cotangent lengths. It is applied in the lemmas that bound cotangent lengths when a flatness condition or a unipotence-on-inertia condition is inserted into or removed from the deformation problem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRep_DeformationRingData_length_cotangent_le_of_level_bounds.lean

import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_DeformationRingData
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Cotangent
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Length
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.BilinearMap

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem GaloisRep.DeformationRingData.length_cotangent_le_of_level_bounds
    {𝒪 : Type} [CommRing 𝒪] [IsDomain 𝒪] [IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) 𝒪]
    {ρbar : ResidualGaloisRep (IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪)}
    {𝒟₀ 𝒟' : ∀ ⦃A : Type⦄ [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [Algebra 𝒪 A], GaloisRepAdic A → Prop}
    (D₀ : GaloisRep.DeformationRingData 𝒪 ρbar 𝒟₀) (D' : GaloisRep.DeformationRingData 𝒪 ρbar 𝒟')
    (θ : D'.R →ₐ[𝒪] D₀.R) (x₀ : D₀.R →ₐ[𝒪] 𝒪) (hθsurj : Function.Surjective θ) (B : ℕ∞)
    (hB : ∀ n : ℕ,
      Module.length 𝒪 (((RingHom.ker (x₀.comp θ : D'.R →ₐ[𝒪] 𝒪)).Cotangent →ₗ[𝒪]
        𝒪 ⧸ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) ^ (n + 1)) ⧸
      LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.lcomp 𝒪 (𝒪 ⧸ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) ^ (n + 1))
        (LinearMap.ker (Ideal.mapCotangent (RingHom.ker (x₀.comp θ : D'.R →ₐ[𝒪] 𝒪))
            (RingHom.ker x₀) θ (fun _ hr => hr))).subtype)) ≤ B) :
    Module.length 𝒪 (RingHom.ker (x₀.comp θ : D'.R →ₐ[𝒪] 𝒪)).Cotangent ≤
      Module.length 𝒪 (RingHom.ker x₀).Cotangent + B := by sorry
